hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18651","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us from Qatadah from Khilas from Abdullah ibn Utbah, he said: Ibn Masud was approached about a man who married a woman, then died leaving her without fixing a dowry for her and without consummating with her, and he was asked about her for a month and said nothing about her, then they asked him, and he said: I shall say about her by my opinion; if it is wrong it is from me and from Satan, and if it is right it is from Allah: she gets the dowry of one of her women, and she has inheritance, and upon her is the waiting period; so a man of Ashja stood and said: I bear witness that you have judged in it with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning Barwa bint Washiq; he said: So he said: Bring your two witnesses, so al-Jarrah and Abu Sinan, two men of Ashja, testified for him."
"18652","Abu Said narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us from Ibrahim from Alqamah and al-Aswad, he said: A people came to Abdullah, meaning Ibn Masud, and said: What do you think about a man who married a woman - then he mentioned the hadith - he said: So a man of Ashja said - Mansur said: I think he is Salamah ibn Yazid - he said: Concerning the like of this the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged; a man of us married a woman of Banu Ruas called Barwa bint Washiq, then he went out on an outing and fell into a well and it became foul and he died, without fixing a dowry for her, so they came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Like the dowry of her women, no reduction and no excess, and she has inheritance, and upon her is the waiting period."
"18653","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Dawud from al-Shabi from Alqamah that a man married a woman, then her husband died leaving her before consummating with her and without naming a dowry for her, and Abdullah was asked about her, and he said: She gets the dowry of one of her women, with no reduction and no excess, and she has inheritance, and upon her is the waiting period; so Abu Sinan al-Ashjai stood among a group of Ashja and said: We bear witness that you have judged in it with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning Barwa bint Washiq."
"18654","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us - Abdullah said: and Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us - from Dawud from al-Shabi from Alqamah with this."
"18655","And Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Shaybah, Abdullah ibn Muhammad, narrated it to us, and he mentioned the hadith."
"18656","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Firas from al-Shabi from Masruq from Abdullah about a man who married a woman, then died leaving her without consummating with her and without fixing a dowry for her, he said: She gets the dowry, and upon her is the waiting period, and she has inheritance; so Maqil ibn Sinan said: I witnessed the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judge with it concerning Barwa bint Washiq."
"18657","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Mansur from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah, like the hadith of Firas."
"18658","Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan informed us from Mansur from Ibrahim from Alqamah, he said: Abdullah was approached about a woman whom a man married, then died without fixing a dowry for her and without consummating with her; he said: So they kept coming to him, and he said: I see for her the like of the dowry of her women, and she has inheritance, and upon her is the waiting period; so Maqil ibn Sinan al-Ashjai testified that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged concerning Barwa bint Washiq with the like of this."
